# No em dashes

Never write the em dash character (`—`, U+2014) in agent-authored text.

## Applies to

- Code comments and docstrings
- UI / user-facing copy agents write or edit
- Docs, ADRs, READMEs, AGENTS.md, skills, and rules agents edit
- Commit messages and PR bodies
- Chat responses when this rule governs output

## Prefer instead

| Intent | Use |
|--------|-----|
| Pause / aside | comma, period, or parentheses |
| Introduce clause | colon |
| Compound / range | hyphen (`-`) or en dash (`–`, U+2013) |

## Examples

- Bad: `Upload source — then generate MCQs`
- Good: `Upload source, then generate MCQs`
- Good: `Upload source: then generate MCQs`

Do not introduce new em dashes. Leave existing ones alone unless you are already editing that sentence.
